      "eyebrow": "Where the risk is",
      "heading": "The kinds of software",
      "html": "<p>\"Construction software\" covers several problems. Fixing the wrong one first is common. Project management tracks jobs, deadlines, people and costs. A 10-person firm can do most of that in a spreadsheet, a calendar and a WhatsApp group. It rarely pays until 20 to 30 staff. Buildertrend and CoConstruct serve that need.</p><p>Documents matter too: drawings, specs, certificates and warranties. Google Drive, Dropbox and OneDrive cover the basics. Procore Documents and Aconex are too much. A tidy shared drive and a naming rule suit most small firms.</p>"
    },
