      "kind": "default",
      "eyebrow": "The real risk",
      "heading": "Site inspections, H&S and plant",
      "html": "<p>This is where the legal risk is. Every contractor on site has inspection and record duties: RAMS (risk assessments and method statements), inductions, toolbox talks, plant pre-use checks, scaffold inspections, near-miss reports. A small firm must make and keep a lot of them.</p><p>Most use paper forms and emailed PDFs. When an auditor asks for last November's site inspections, the answer is often an apology. Plant sits alongside: which plant is on which site, when it was last checked, when the next PUWER inspection is due. A spreadsheet of expiry dates works for a small fleet.</p>"
