      "html": "<p><strong>iAuditor (SafetyCulture)</strong> is the global leader. Many templates, strong reports, an app, and a price per seat that grows with every person added. It suits a larger contractor with an H&S manager to own it. For a 10-person firm without one, it is hard to set up and use falls short.</p><p><strong>GoAudits</strong> was founded in the UK. It is often pitched as iAuditor for less. Flexible templates, UK support, but an app and login are still needed. Better value, same risk: people who disliked one app may dislike this one.</p><p><strong>Paper and email</strong> are the quiet default. Free, no fuss, works without signal. But nothing is searchable, and filing grows with every job. Paper fails an audit when records from 18 months ago are wanted. It is a backup, not a system.</p>"
